/// ZIP archives (the format `PKZIP` defined in APPNOTE.TXT), presented the way
/// Python's `zipfile` module presents them.
///
///     zipfile.ZipFile(file, mode, compression, allowZip64, compresslevel)
///     zipfile.ZipInfo(name, date_time)
///     zipfile.is_zipfile(source)
///     zipfile.ZIP_STORED / ZIP_DEFLATED / ZIP_BZIP2 / ZIP_LZMA
///
/// Reading walks the central directory and decompresses a member on demand;
/// writing records the members and lays down the local headers, the central
/// directory and the end-of-central-directory record when `close()` runs.
/// `ZIP_DEFLATED` members go through `koala/zlib`, so a stored and a deflated
/// member produce the same bytes Python produces.
///
///     let zf = zipfile.ZipFile("out.zip", "w", zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED)
///     zf.writestr("hello.txt", "hello world")
///     zf.close()
///     let zr = zipfile.ZipFile("out.zip")
///     print(zr.namelist())              // [hello.txt]
///     print(zr.read("hello.txt"))       // b"hello world"
///     zr.close()
///
/// Three Python details cannot be carried over, and the difference is
/// deliberate:
///   - `ZIP_BZIP2` and `ZIP_LZMA` are declared but not implemented: Koala has
///     no bzip2 or LZMA codec, so both panic with a message that says so.
///   - `with` does not exist, so `close()` is explicit (it is idempotent);
///     for a file opened for writing, `close()` is what creates the archive.
///   - The constructor parameter names differ where Koala rejects a parameter
///     that shadows a field (`ZipInfo(name, date_time)` is `ZipInfo(arcname,
///     dt)` here); call sites pass these positionally and are unaffected.
///
/// Encryption (`pwd`), `zipfile.Path` and Python's `ZipExtFile`-returning
/// `open()` are not offered.